{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#450","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#450","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#450\",\"parent_revision\":\"9affdab503aa4e1e409a060b89b507d39eb583a1\",\"root_revision\":\"4f0726f21e63670fe14c354e1915074f5a8e2928b55782e35027c7fd0597c907\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWhen implement-feature retries a BLOCKED task, the delegated agent receives the same prompt as the first attempt with no signal that this is a retry. The agent has no basis to try a different strategy, ask different questions, or be more conservative.\\n\\nSymphony passes `attempt` (null on first run, integer on retry) to the Liquid prompt template, and continuation turns receive only continuation guidance \u2014 not the full original prompt.\\n\\n**Proposed behaviour:**\\n- When implement-feature dispatches a task with RetryCount > 0, prepend to the delegation prompt:\\n  ```\\n  This is attempt {N} for task {task_id}. The previous attempt did not complete successfully.\\n  Review what was attempted (check git log, modified files) before choosing a new approach.\\n  ```\\n- For tasks with a previous BLOCKED note (from stall detection or agent failure), include the note text in the retry prompt so the agent knows why it was blocked.\\n- Task file: add `LastFailureReason` field populated by the hook or orchestrator on failure.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria:**\\n- Retry delegation prompt includes attempt number and last failure reason.\\n- First-attempt prompts are not modified (no attempt context injected).\\n- LastFailureReason is readable in `implementation_manager.py status` output.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | Task dispatch code path in implement-feature skill | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/` |\\n| 2 | `implementation_manager.py` with retry/stall detection | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` |\\n| 3 | SAM task data format (knows which fields exist) | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/task_format.py` |\\n| 4 | How RetryCount is tracked and where stall detection writes BLOCKED notes | DERIVABLE | Inspect `implementation_manager.py` around stall detection |\\n| 5 | Where delegation prompt is constructed (Liquid template or Python) | DERIVABLE | Search implement-feature skill for prompt construction |\\n| 6 | Backward-compat strategy for tasks without LastFailureReason | DERIVABLE | Follows same pattern as other optional task fields |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all information is available or derivable from the codebase.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **pass attempt count to agent on task retry** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: OpenAI Symphony SPEC.md \u2014 prompt template receives `attempt` variable: null on first run, integer on retry; continuation turns receive only continuation guidance, not full original prompt\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Affects implement-feature skill dispatch path and implementation_manager.py retry logic. No external API changes. Risk is low \u2014 change is additive; existing tasks without the new field must be handled gracefully with a default value.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- When `implement-feature` dispatches a task with `RetryCount > 0`, the delegation prompt is prepended with: `This is attempt {N} for task {task_id}. The previous attempt did not complete successfully. Review what was attempted (check git log, modified files) before choosing a new approach.`\\n- When the previous attempt ended with a BLOCKED note (from stall detection or agent failure), that note text is included in the retry prompt\\n- First-attempt prompts are not modified \u2014 no attempt context is injected when RetryCount == 0\\n- A `LastFailureReason` field is added to the task data structure and populated by the orchestrator on failure\\n- `implementation_manager.py status` output displays `LastFailureReason` when set\\n- Regression: existing tasks without `LastFailureReason` are handled gracefully (field defaults to empty string or None)\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/` \u2014 task dispatch logic, delegation prompt construction\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` \u2014 stall detection, retry orchestration, status output\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/task_format.py` \u2014 add `LastFailureReason` field to task data model\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 document `LastFailureReason` field\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an implement-feature orchestrator, I need retry attempts to include attempt number and last failure reason in the delegation prompt so the agent can try a different strategy instead of repeating the same failed approach.\\n\",\"digest\":\"1f6e19b5cdd8d2b35511b352dfe78c9432e335b525ddff65b676c1c8ba975743\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg00eQ\"}"}